===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|lappe}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|lappo}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*lappa-}}. The form is remarkable because of the unshifted geminate ''-pp-'' (instead of expected Old High German *''lapfo''). Based on the supposedly invariable nature of the consonant shift, {{m|goh||lappo}} would have to be an originally [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] form (compare {{etyl|osx|de}} {{m|osx|lappo}}). This is, however, quite unlikely since the Old High German word is attested as early as the 9th century, and no variants with ''-pf-'' exist. The form remains thus unexplained.

